(JavaScript Basics for Document Q&A) Tj T*
T*
(Version: 1.0) Tj T*
(Audience: new developers building browser or Node.js apps) Tj T*
(Purpose: provide a compact, searchable document for testing a RAG chatbot.) Tj T*
T*
(1. What JavaScript Is) Tj T*
T*
(JavaScript is a programming language used to make web pages interactive and to build) Tj T*
(server applications with Node.js. In the browser, JavaScript can respond to clicks,) Tj T*
(update page content, validate forms, and call APIs. In Node.js, JavaScript can read) Tj T*
(files, run web servers, access databases, and automate tasks.) Tj T*
T*
(JavaScript is single-threaded at the language level, but it can handle many waiting) Tj T*
(tasks with an event loop. The event loop lets JavaScript continue running while timers,) Tj T*
(network requests, and file operations are waiting for results.) Tj T*
T*
(2. Variables and Values) Tj T*
T*
(Use const by default when a variable should not be reassigned. Use let when the value) Tj T*
(needs to change later. Avoid var in modern code because it has function scope and can) Tj T*
(create confusing behavior.) Tj T*
T*
(Example:) Tj T*
T*
(```js) Tj T*
(const userName = "Mina";) Tj T*
(let loginCount = 1;) Tj T*
(loginCount = loginCount + 1;) Tj T*
(```) Tj T*
T*
(Common JavaScript value types include strings, numbers, booleans, null, undefined,) Tj T*
(arrays, objects, and functions. A string stores text. A number stores numeric values. A) Tj T*
(boolean is either true or false. Null means an intentional empty value. Undefined) Tj T*
(usually means a value has not been assigned yet.) Tj T*
T*
(3. Functions) Tj T*
T*
(A function groups reusable logic. Functions can receive input through parameters and) Tj T*
(return output with the return keyword.) Tj T*
T*
(Example:) Tj T*
T*
(```js) Tj T*
(function greet\(name\) {) Tj T*
(  return Hello, ${name};) Tj T*
(}) Tj T*
T*
ET
