(4. Arrays and Objects) Tj T*
T*
(An array stores an ordered list of values. Use array methods like map, filter, find, and) Tj T*
(reduce to transform or search lists.) Tj T*
T*
(Example:) Tj T*
T*
(```js) Tj T*
(const scores = [8, 12, 15];) Tj T*
(const passed = scores.filter\(\(score\) => score >= 10\);) Tj T*
(```) Tj T*
T*
(An object stores named properties. Objects are useful for representing things like) Tj T*
(users, products, messages, or settings.) Tj T*
T*
(Example:) Tj T*
T*
(```js) Tj T*
(const user = {) Tj T*
(  id: 42,) Tj T*
(  name: "Leila",) Tj T*
(  role: "admin") Tj T*
(};) Tj T*
(```) Tj T*
T*
(Use dot notation when the property name is known, such as user.name. Use bracket) Tj T*
(notation when the property name is stored in a variable, such as user[fieldName].) Tj T*
T*
