(6. Async JavaScript) Tj T*
T*
(Asynchronous code handles work that finishes later, such as calling an API or reading a) Tj T*
(file. A Promise represents a future result. Use async and await to write Promise-based) Tj T*
(code in a readable style.) Tj T*
T*
(Example:) Tj T*
T*
(```js) Tj T*
(async function loadUser\(userId\) {) Tj T*
(  const response = await fetch\(/api/users/${userId}\);) Tj T*
(  const user = await response.json\(\);) Tj T*
(  return user;) Tj T*
(}) Tj T*
(```) Tj T*
T*
(Use try and catch to handle errors in async functions:) Tj T*
T*
(```js) Tj T*
(try {) Tj T*
(  const user = await loadUser\(42\);) Tj T*
(  console.log\(user.name\);) Tj T*
(} catch \(error\) {) Tj T*
(  console.error\("Could not load user", error\);) Tj T*
(}) Tj T*
(```) Tj T*
T*
