(8. Node.js and npm) Tj T*
T*
(Node.js lets JavaScript run outside the browser. Express.js is a popular Node.js) Tj T*
(framework for building APIs. npm is the package manager used to install libraries and) Tj T*
(run scripts.) Tj T*
T*
(Common npm commands:) Tj T*
T*
(- npm install installs project dependencies.) Tj T*
(- npm run dev runs the development script defined in package.json.) Tj T*
(- npm run build creates a production build when the project supports it.) Tj T*
T*
(In Node.js projects, environment variables are often stored in a .env file during) Tj T*
(development. API keys should not be committed to git.) Tj T*
T*
(9. Debugging Checklist) Tj T*
T*
(When JavaScript code fails, check the error message first. Then confirm the line number,) Tj T*
(inspect variable values, and simplify the failing code path. In browser apps, use the) Tj T*
(developer console and the network tab. In Node.js apps, use console logs, stack traces,) Tj T*
(and request logs.) Tj T*
T*
(Useful questions:) Tj T*
T*
(- Is the variable defined before it is used?) Tj T*
(- Is the function receiving the input shape it expects?) Tj T*
(- Did an async function need await?) Tj T*
(- Did the API return an error response?) Tj T*
(- Is the environment variable loaded?) Tj T*
T*
(10. Mini Project: Document Q&A Chatbot) Tj T*
T*
(The chatbot project has two main parts: ingestion and question answering. Ingestion) Tj T*
(loads a PDF, extracts text, splits text into chunks, embeds those chunks, and stores) Tj T*
(them in a vector store. Question answering embeds the user question, retrieves relevant) Tj T*
(chunks, sends those chunks to an LLM, and returns an answer with sources.) Tj T*
T*
(For a first version, use one sample PDF and an in-memory vector store. This makes the) Tj T*
(app easier to understand before adding persistent storage. Later, replace the in-memory) Tj T*
(store with Chroma, Pinecone, Postgres pgvector, or another persistent vector database.) Tj T*
T*
ET
