(The backend should expose endpoints for health checks, indexing the sample document,) Tj T*
(uploading a document, checking index status, and asking a question. The frontend should) Tj T*
(provide a document control area, an upload control, and a chat interface.) Tj T*
T*
(11. Glossary) Tj T*
T*
(Chunk: a smaller section of a document used for retrieval.) Tj T*
T*
(Embedding: a numeric representation of text meaning.) Tj T*
T*
(Vector store: a database or in-memory structure that searches embeddings by similarity.) Tj T*
T*
(Retriever: a component that finds relevant chunks for a query.) Tj T*
T*
(RAG: retrieval-augmented generation, a pattern where an LLM answers using retrieved) Tj T*
(context.) Tj T*
T*
(Prompt: the instruction and context sent to an LLM.) Tj T*
T*
(Hallucination: an answer that sounds confident but is not supported by the provided) Tj T*
(source material.) Tj T*
T*
(12. Recommended First Questions) Tj T*
T*
(Ask these questions to test the chatbot:) Tj T*
T*
(- What is the difference between const, let, and var?) Tj T*
(- How does async and await help with API calls?) Tj T*
(- What are the main steps in a Document Q&A chatbot?) Tj T*
(- Why should a first version use an in-memory vector store?) Tj T*
(- What should I check when JavaScript code fails?) Tj T*
T*
ET
